{"author":{"id":"b409816c5cd5ab140d1d52eb33aace35de44952bb794b19806fd57f6ecb1ace9"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1791395326,"nonce":"/zNCK75dwd4Y7y2CLShSG3KlGuQ=","title":"HIR: reuse proven loads across bounds-check control flow for Cranelift","message":"Objective: make Cranelift competitive with optimized LLVM while avoiding LLVM promotion cost in short runs. Evaluate new shared HIR/Cranelift work with LLVM disabled, interpreter-first entry retained, total process wall time including added optimization cost, and the existing LLVM-enabled build as the speed reference. Do not optimize LLVM compilation as the primary goal.\n\nThe existing load_cse pass forgets every available load at a basic-block boundary. Dynamic list access expands into bounds/error diamonds, leaving repeated header/data loads even when no path writes overlapping memory. Extend existing byte-range/type proofs across CFG edges. Intersect predecessor availability using the same dominating SSA load, discard information at unvisited/backedge predecessors, preserve calls/unknown writes/volatile barriers, derive edges from actual terminators, and bound retained state to protect startup. This does not speculate about runtime types or add frontend kernel special cases.\n\nCranelift alias regions were inspected first: missing regions are their own disjoint category, not an alias-everything fallback. Pairwise HIR proofs cannot simply become region tags on selected instructions while leaving unknown accesses untouched. Cross-block HIR load reuse uses the existing conservative proof rules instead.\n\nValidate branch-arm mutation, join dominance, loops/backedge writes, aliased parameters, volatile loads, host callbacks, and disjoint field writes through interpreter/Cranelift/LLVM. Accept only with checksum-correct LLVM-off NUC gains, including short-run wall time; keep before, same-executable disabled/enabled, and current LLVM reference arms distinct. Baseline commit 9bc3fcd033db1b8a15f0a5d86315fba7be97c5c7, saved NUC binaries /home/raikage/zyntax-perf-binaries/9bc3fcd0/{zypy,zylua}.","files":null}]}